Description: Port the 1995 Unix sources to C99, ncurses and modern Linux
 Converts the K&R C sources to prototyped C99 and fixes the defects that
 stop the game working correctly on a current Linux system:
 .
  * ioctl(FIONREAD) read into a long, picking up garbage high bytes on LP64.
  * fflush(stdin) used as a keyboard flush, which is undefined behaviour.
  * usleep(1800000) exceeded the permitted argument range.
  * selectspeed() fell off the end of the function without returning.
  * The score file was hardcoded to an unwritable path under /usr/games/lib;
    it is now per-user under $HOME, so no setgid binary is needed.
  * Cookie messages were drawn on line 25 and invisible on an 80x24 terminal.
  * The TAGGED shadow matrix was not cleared between games.
  * The link line ignored LDFLAGS, dropping distribution hardening flags.
 .
 Game logic, scoring, screen layout and timing are unchanged.
Author: Bob Easthope <bob@mathscircle.com>
Last-Update: 2026-11-04

